==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Hell Sentinel Emma''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Hell Commissioner Emma''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is quite unusual as she is a tank with many knockbacks, meaning that she will stay alive for a long time while also remaining in the frontline most of the time, also thanks to her speed. This helps her performance as a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]], as, unlike [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]], she will not stay in the frontline alone, taking hits until death, but, instead, she will let herself be pushed back, thus allowing her to live longer and protect other units for longer as well.

Similar to [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]], Emma will constantly come back immediately after being knocked back. The main difference is that she stands far enough back to outrange most [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]]. Her main weakness is that when enemies start pushing, she will inevitably get knocked back, potentially letting a wave slip by. However this is also her greatest strength. Most other Wave Shields will simply die or take a lot of damage when an enemy starts attacking them. On the other hand, Emma will survive while taking very low damage. She's capable of taking up to 25,500 damage before getting knocked back, which isn't tanky, but would be a standard amount for a unit with lower health.

==='''True Form'''===
Emma's notable gains in True Form include increased Weaken chance, greater health, Freeze and Warp Immunity. She still can't be used as a Tank due to having a high knockback count, but having more health does make things better, and Freeze Immunity ensures she can't be disabled by such attacks. Warp Immunity is situational, since she isn't all that compatible against those that employ it. The Weaken improvement remains unreliable, but having a higher activation chance does improve her survivability and those of other units when they occur, while allowing her to block waves better. If you do have more consistent Anti-Wave units, Emma's expensive True Form might not even be needed and could be easily passed up; her role as a Weaken based Tank however with her Cat Combo including [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] is a possible eye-opener if you have the three required to use it especially if you frequently use [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]; boosting Weaken duration by a whole 30%, which can be a saving grace on many occasions.

==='''Talents'''===
Starting with '''Wave Attack''', Emma's Multi-Hit almost ensures that at least one Wave will be fired per attack cycle, which can help with clearing weak peons and chipping enemies in the backline. She only has a 16% chance at best to land both a Wave and Weaken proc on any of her hits, but when they do activate simultaneously, they can significantly hamper the enemy's ability to progress while the effect lasts.

At its maximum level, her '''Weaken''' Talent can nearly ''double'' the duration of the ability. It still won't be guaranteed to trigger every attack cycle, but the Talent will at least make it dramatically easier for her to keep the effect active for most of the time that she's out.

'''Curse Immunity''' of course is immensely useful in Uncanny Legends stages and those after, and should absolutely be considered if she sees frequent usage by that point of the game.

Due to Emma's damage output being rather low even with the Wave Attack Talent unlocked, '''Attack Buff''' can be skipped without losing out on much in regards to her performance. '''HP Buff''' on the other hand can greatly benefit her, as even at level 30 her health would increase by nearly 70,000 points, or over 100,000 by the time she hits level 50.

==='''Orb'''===
As she is a universal tank/crowd controller with mediocre damage, it's best to simply give her a spare Defense Orb for whatever trait you find yourself using her against most often.

{{Job|Classification = Tanker & Crowd-Controller}}

